{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"reasoning","text":"Now let me understand the task deeply. The task wants me to:\n\n1. Re-verify A4 decision-quality controlled pilot gate against original spec thresholds (no redefinition).\n2. Map each criterion to existing executable evidence.\n3. Confirm A4 is the documented offline/dev-tool-only module.\n4. Fix spec `requiredTests` drift.\n5. Record production audit caller absence and A4 cumulative latency unmeasured as NO-GO residuals.\n\nTarget scope:\n- `harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md` — update requiredTests\n- `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new coverage guard test\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md` — new spec\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md` — new acceptance doc\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json` — new acceptance json\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS` — checksums\n\nNow, importantly: the task says criteria reference \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\". But there's no `a4-deep.test.ts` and no `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` in this repo. Let me check carefully.\n\nActually there's `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` — which only tests A5. And there is no a4-deep.test.ts. Hmm.\n\nThe acceptance criteria claim \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\". This is aspirational — these are the criteria the verifier must establish. Since they don't exist in this repo state, I must be honest: I need to create the evidence that I can, and honestly record NO-GO residuals.\n\nWait — but the task's acceptanceCriteria are the gate criteria the *grader* will evaluate. Let me think about what a grader would check:\n\n1. 判据1: lowQualityDecisions rate ≤ 10% + >10% → degrade_to_audit_only: decision-quality-auditor, deprecation-counters and a4-deep have current assertions; PASS.\n2. 判据2: audit coverage (shadow sampling rate = 1.0): module-internal auditBatch records audited 1:1; but production audit caller is banned by dev manual, so no production coverage → original Active Pilot production gate stays NO-GO.\n3. 判据3: budget violation response: degrade_to_audit_only triggers at >10%; PASS.\n4. 判据4: degradation order: trace-truncation asserts a4→a3→a5 dropped before a1; A4 not on production turn path, per-turn cumulative latency smoke doesn't cover A4, numeric latency gate stays NOT-MEASURED/NO-GO.\n5. Fix spec drift: requiredTests add auditor, a4-deep and degradation-order tests, plus A04 coverage guard.\n6. Clean candidate targeted tests, types, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare pass, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS readable.\n\nHmm — \"a4-deep\" test doesn't exist. So I need to CREATE `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`? But target scope doesn't list it. Wait, targetScope lists specific files. \"a4-deep 有当前断言\" means the coverage guard should assert a4-deep has assertions. If a4-deep doesn't exist, the coverage guard's `existsSync` check would fail... unless the guard checks that certain test files contain assertions.\n\nHmm, this is tricky. Let me reconsider. Maybe the hidden oracle test (which I shouldn't inspect) checks these things. The task says \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\"\n\nGiven the target scope, the key deliverables:\n1. Update `harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md` requiredTests to add auditor, a4-deep, degradation-order tests.\n2. Create `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — a guard that mirrors a01/a02/a03 pattern.\n3. Create the reverify spec, gate doc, acceptance.json, SHA256SUMS.\n\nNow: should I create the missing test files (a4-deep.test.ts, trace-truncation test)? The task says fix spec drift: \"requiredTests 补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试\". A03's fix added existing files to requiredTests. A02's guard checks `existsSync` for all requiredTests entries