tent for exact content and be careful.\n\nLet me now check the release-source-manifest to find `ln.test.ts` real name.\n\nLet me now verify: does `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts` exist? No (confirmed: deep dir has only a1,a2,a3). Does the manifest mention it as expected? Let me check.\n\nAnyway. Let me focus: I'll create the evidence needed and honestly document. Let me check the manifest reference and the o02-acceptance references to a4-deep.\n\nLet me be systematic and gather the remaining facts:\n1. What does `release-source-manifest.json` say about `tests/unit/deep/ln.test.ts`?\n2. Does `harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md` reference a4-deep?\n3. What's in `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/o02-acceptance.json` re a4?\n\nLet me also check git for the base commit — but there's no .git. The task says baseCommit 65ecf51.... and \"SHA256SUMS 可回读\" (readable). \n\nLet me look at the baseline-evidence.json and ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS to see if a4 entries existed.\n\nActually, given constraints (no network, no node_modules), I cannot run vitest. So \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\" — I can run node scripts, sha256, tsc? tsc needs node_modules (typescript). Hmm. Let me check if typescript is available globally.\n\nGiven no node_modules, I likely can't run vitest/tsc/eslint. So \"relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\" would be: SHA256SUMS verification (sha256sum via certutil/Get-FileHash), JSON validity checks, harness validate (needs node_modules? let me check harness scripts), credential scan (file-based).\n\nLet me check if `pnpm harness` works without install. Probably not (it's a local script). Let me check scripts/.\n\nLet me proceed step by step. First gather remaining facts."}}
