.ts` doesn't exist! It's referenced by a1/a2/a3 specs as requiredTests. Hmm, but A03's accept doc says performance-budgets passed... Let me double-check. Actually wait — the test file `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` doesn't exist. Let me verify by listing.\n\nActually, the A03 coverage test asserts `read(\"tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\")` contains \"p99\". If it didn't exist, that test would throw. But A03 was \"completed\"... but tests may not have been run after the workspace was stripped. Actually the task explicitly says \"Do not install dependencies\" so I can't run vitest. The environment seems to have removed node_modules.\n\nHmm, but the A03 acceptance says 72 tests passed and 3 coverage tests passed. Perhaps the harness stripped some test files to make this task's drift real. Let me check which required test files exist vs not.\n\nLet me carefully enumerate the requiredTests referenced across specs and check existence."}}
