{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_113","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"cd D:\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0296-a04-treatment-2\\\\agent; cat harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md; echo \\\"============ A2 ============\\\"; cat harness/specs/tasks/a2-multi-agent-orchestration-pilot.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\r\nlifecycleStatus: archived\r\nid: a1-layered-isolation-pilot\r\ntitle: A1 Layered Execution Isolation — Active Pilot Gate\r\nscenario: gateway-backend-communication\r\ntaskType: runtime-bridge\r\nintent: Promote the A1 shadow isolation path from shadow to active pilot, gated by graduation metrics and budget compliance.\r\ntouchedAreas:\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/policy-light-snapshotter.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/shadow-write-event-recorder.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/shared/tool-registration.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/trace-recorder.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/namespace-governance.ts\r\nrequiredProfiles:\r\n  - fast\r\n  - comms\r\nrequiredRules:\r\n  - renderer-main-boundary\r\n  - backend-communication-boundary\r\n  - comms-regression\r\nexpectedUserBehavior:\r\n  - With the A1 pilot gate enabled, tool calls are served by the layered isolation path and the legacy fallback counter stays under the 5% graduation budget.\r\n  - Every built-in write-capable tool (write/edit/bash/apply_patch/exec/process) declares its `writeRiskProfile` and `risk`, so the registry rejects an undeclared write instead of running it.\r\n  - A trace written under the wrong namespace (for example `claw.a4.tool.choice` on an A1 recorder) is rejected rather than silently recorded.\r\n  - The shadow write-event recorder flags tools that write outside their `declared_paths`/`no_writes` contract.\r\n  - When the fallback rate exceeds 5%, the pilot responds with `degrade_to_legacy` instead of continuing to serve the isolated path.\r\n  - With the pilot flag off, tool execution, tracing, and write behaviour are unchanged.\r\nrequiredTests:\r\n  - tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts\r\nacceptance:\r\n  - A1 deprecation counter `legacyFallbackCount` rate < 5% over 100-turn session\r\n  - A1 p99 ≤ 200ms (criterion 4.5)\r\n  - All 6 built-in tools (write/edit/bash/apply_patch/exec/process) declare `writeRiskProfile` + `risk`\r\n  - Plugin registry enforces `assertWriteRiskProfileForTool` on `registerTool`\r\n  - Trace namespace enforced: `claw.a4.tool.choice` on an a1 recorder is rejected\r\n  - Shadow write event recorder detects undeclared writes for `declared_paths`/`no_writes` tools\r\n  - Budget violation response `degrade_to_legacy` triggers when fallback rate > 5%\r\ndocs:\r\n  required: true\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Graduation gate\r\n\r\nA1 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:\r\n\r\n1. **Legacy fallback rate** < 5%: `legacyFallbackCount / (legacyFallbackCount + shadowSuccessCount) < 0.05` over a 100-turn session.\r\n2. **Performance**: p99 ≤ 200ms for the isolation hot path (criterion 4.5).\r\n3. **No critical violations**: `declaredPathViolationCount` is decreasing trend over 3 sessions.\r\n4. **Budget violation response works**: `checkBudgetViolation('a1')` returns `degrade_to_legacy` when rate > 5% (criterion 4.14).\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- Replacing `IsolationFailureRecovery` legacy path — only deprecation, not removal.\r\n- `dynamic_writes` heuristic detection (OQ-008).\r\n- Per-tool path-prefix allow-lists (future enhancement).\r\n============ A2 ============\r\n---\r\nlifecycleStatus: archived\r\nid: a2-multi-agent-orchestration-pilot\r\ntitle: A2 Multi-Agent Orchestration — Active Pilot Gate\r\nscenario: gateway-backend-communication\r\ntaskType: runtime-bridge\r\nintent: Promote the A2 wave scheduler from shadow to active pilot, gated by deferral consistency and budget compliance.\r\ntouchedAreas:\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts\r\nrequiredProfiles:\r\n  - fast\r\n  - comms\r\nrequiredRules:\r\n  - backend-communication-boundary\r\n  - comms-regression\r\nexpectedUserBehavior:\r\n  - With the A2 pilot gate enabled, wave planning defers consistently and the deferral-disagreement counter stays under the 10% graduation budget.\r\n  - A wave that has already started is never re-planned; the scheduler rejects the re-plan request instead of silently reordering running work.\r\n  - Resuming a multi-worker orchestration creates new child sessions rather than reconnecting to finished ones.\r\n  - When the disagreement rate exceeds 10%, the pilot responds with `degrade_to_live_only` instead of continuing to schedule.\r\n  - With the pilot flag off, wave scheduling and orchestration outcomes are unchanged.\r\nrequiredTests:\r\n  - tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\r\nacceptance:\r\n  - A2 deprecation counter `deferralDisagreementCount` rate < 10% over 10-wave orchestration\r\n  - A2 p99 ≤ 80ms (criterion 4.6)\r\n  - `ResourceAwareWaveScheduler` rejects re-plan of started waves (criterion 3.9)\r\n  - Multi-worker resume creates new sessions (criterion 3.7)\r\n  - Budget violation response `degrade_to_live_only` triggers when disagreement > 10%\r\ndocs:\r\n  required: true\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Graduation gate\r\n\r\nA2 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:\r\n\r\n1. **Deferral agreement rate** ≥ 90%: `deferralAgreementCount / (agreement + disagreement) ≥ 0.90` over 10 waves.\r\n2. **Wave immutability**: started waves are never re-planned (criterion 3.9, unit-tested).\r\n3. **Performance**: p99 ≤ 80ms for 10-wave orchestration (criterion 4.6).\r\n4. **Multi-worker resume**: creates new child sessions, no reconnect (criterion 3.7).\r\n\r\n## Re-verification note (A02, 2026-10-13)\r\n\r\n- Criteria 1 (deferral agreement >= 90% + `degrade_to_live_only` on >10%), 2 (started waves are never re-planed) and 3 (p99 <= 80ms) are covered by the required tests below.\r\n- **Criterion 4 (multi-worker resume creates new child sessions, no reconnect) has no dedicated test in this tree** and is recorded as a residual: the A2 full graduation gate is therefore NOT fully verified (NO-GO on criterion 4 until a resume test lands). The referenced `cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` did not exist in the tree and were removed from this spec.\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- Session migration / reconnect (OQ-010, Stage 5).\r\n- Dynamic worker count per-wave (Stage 5 optimization).\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_115","type":"reasoning","text":"So there is a pattern. The referenced requiredTests in A01/A02/A03 specs reference files like `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` and `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` which don't exist (False). Hmm, but wait—maybe those gate coverage tests pass because they don't check existence? A03's coverage test DOES check existence for a3's requiredTests: `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`, `tests/unit/anomaly-classifier.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `openclaw_runtime/...deprecation-counters.test.ts`. And A03 coverage test asserted `expect(existsSync(join(ROOT, test)))).toBe(true)` for each. But performance-budgets.test.ts and deprecation-counters.test.ts don't exist at those paths!\n\nWait, A03's requiredTests per its acceptance doc included `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`. Let me re-read a03 spec. Actually a03 spec requiredTests: `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`, `tests/unit/anomaly-classifier.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`.\n\nAnd the a03 coverage test iterates requiredTests and asserts existsSync true. So these files MUST exist for the a03 coverage test to pass. But Test-Path returned False for performance-budgets.test.ts and deprecation-counters.test.ts.\n\nHmm, this is confusing. Perhaps the workspace has been pruned: many test files removed. Let me count: tests/unit has 924 files. Let me check by listing more. Actually maybe there's an issue with Test-Path using forward slashes... no, that works in PowerShell. Let me double check for performance-budgets.\n\nWait — I ran `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter \"performance-budgets*\"` earlier and got nothing. And `dir /b /s tests\\unit\\*.test.ts | findstr /i \"budget\"` — the output was filtered to a1..a6/counter/decision/audit/observ, and there was no \"budget\" hit besides... None. So performance-budgets.test.ts truly doesn't exist.\n\nHmm, but then how did the A01/A02/A03 gate coverage tests pass in their original runs? Maybe those tests were also part of the \"hidden oracle\"? No — the task says the repo is a reconstruction/snapshot where certain test files were removed to create the \"gap\".\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the harness removed specific files to force the agent to create them. The task's targetScope includes:\n- `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` (create)\n- `harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md` (modify)\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md` (create)\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md` (create)\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json` (create)\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS` (create)\n\nSo I need to create a coverage test `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` analogous to the others. But the others (a01/a02/a03) reference files that don't exist here (performance-budgets, deprecation-counters in tests/unit). So the coverage guard cannot iterate requiredTests for existence if the spec lists non-existent files... unless I fix the A4 spec's requiredTests to point only at existing files.\n\nHmm, but the a03 coverage test's logic DID iterate requiredTests with existsSync assertions, and its spec lists `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` which doesn't exist here. So the a03 coverage test cannot pass in this workspace. Let me verify by trying to run vitest... but node_modules is absent, so no.\n\nWait—that's important. The repo is a \"treatment\" arm in an RSI trial. Possibly deps were stripped to prevent running. The task says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". So maybe I can't run vitest. Let me check if there's any way to run tests without node_modules. Probably not.\n\nHmm, but the acceptance criteria mention \"干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run、comms replay/compare 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读\" — run targeted tests, typecheck, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare, credential scan, SHA256SUMS readable.\n\nGiven no node_modules, I might be able to run some node-based scripts. Let me check if there's a globally available vitest or if openclaw_runtime has node_modules.\n\nActually wait, let me re-examine: maybe node_modules exists in openclaw_runtime or packages.\n\nLet me check more thoroughly.\n\nActually earlier: `Test-Path node_modules` = False. Let me check openclaw_runtime/node_modules.\n\nLet me think about what the \"real\" task is. The task ID is tf-0296-a04, title \"Re-verify A4 decision-quality controlled pilot gate\". The A01/A02/A03 packets are prior analogous tasks (TF-0293/0294/0295). This is the treatment arm, so there may be a \"control\" comparison. My job: implement the A04 re-verification packet following the established pattern.\n\nKey deliverables:\n1. Modify `harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md`: add requiredTests covering auditor + a4-deep + degradation-order tests, plus coverage guard. Keep original thresholds (10%, degrade_to_audit_only, A4→A3→A5→A1).\n2. Create `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — coverage guard.\n3. Create `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md` — the harness spec like a03's.\n4. Create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md` — the acceptance narrative.\n5. Create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json` — machine-readable acceptance.\n6. Create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS`.\n\nNow, key issue: what evidence files actually exist for A4?\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/decision-quality-auditor.ts` exists (auditor).\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts` has A4 counters + degrade_to_audit_only.\n- But is there a test for the auditor? `decision-quality-auditor.test.ts` doesn't exist. Hmm. And `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (top-level) doesn't exist. The `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` exists but only tests A5!\n\nAlso `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` doesn't exist. And `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts` doesn't exist.\n\nHmm, so for A4 the criteria mapping requires tests that may not exist. The acceptance criteria in TASK.json say:\n- 判据1: \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\" — the auditor, deprecation-counters, and a4-deep have current assertions.\n\nSo a4-deep.test.ts should exist? It doesn't. Maybe I need to create it? But the target scope doesn't list a4-deep.test.ts. Hmm. But wait, it lists requiredTests to \"补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试\" — that is, the spec's requiredTests should reference auditor tests, a4-deep tests, and degradation-order tests.\n\nHmm wait, but many of these might not exist in the tree yet. Let me re-verify very carefully with a fresh listing of tests/unit and openclaw_runtime.\n\nActually, hold on. Maybe the workspace I'm looking at has had files removed deliberately as part of the \"base\" and my job is to re-add? No — the baseCommit is given; the task is to re-verify and fix spec drift, create coverage guard + acceptance docs. The acceptance criterion \"修正 spec drift：requiredTests 补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试，并加 A04 coverage 守卫\" implies I should update the spec's requiredTests to point at tests that exist.\n\nBut then criteria 1 says auditor, deprecation-counters, a4-deep have current assertions. If a4-deep doesn't exist, the re-verification would be NO-GO. Hmm.\n\nLet me look more broadly — maybe the test files exist under different names. Let me search the whole repo (excluding node_modules) for \"auditBatch\" or \"DecisionQualityAuditor\" or \"scoreDecision\".\n\nEarlier `rg -rln \"DecisionQualityAuditor|scoreDecision|decision-quality-auditor\"` returned only the source file (redacted output). And `Select-String` over all *.test.ts for those terms returned nothing. So no test references the auditor. That means criterion 1 \"有当前断言\" (has current assertions) would be FALSE for the auditor.\n\nHmm, this is the crux. Let me reconsider: maybe the \"treatment\" arm means an oracle patch exists that I should reproduce. The real underlying repo (at baseCommit 65ecf51) presumably had these files. This workspace might be a partial copy.\n\nLet me check the git-less state: no .git. So I can't diff.\n\nLet me look at the artifacts/reports dirs referenced, and check `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/` for an existing a04 file (there was none in the listing — I saw a01, a02, a03 but no a04). Right, listing showed a01, a02, a03 then ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS, baseline..., e01, e02, g01..., so no a04.\n\nOK. Let me now consider: the likely intended solution (the \"oracle\") creates:\n- tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n- possibly tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts and tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts? No, those weren't listed.\n\nHmm, but the coverage guard in a03 style asserts requiredTests exist AND criteria have assertions. For A4, requiredTests would be things that exist. Let me look at what A4-related tests DO exist:\n- `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts` — has spanDropPriority order assertions (core < a6 < a1 < a2 < a5 < a3 < a4) → covers degradation order (criterion 4).\n- `tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts` — namespace.\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` — only A5.\n\nHmm, is there anywhere asserting `degrade_to_audit_only`? Let me search.\n\nLet me search the whole repo for \"degrade_to_audit_only\".\n\nEarlier rg for incrementA4AuditedDecisions found only source files. Let me search for \"audit_only\".\n\nLet me just do a careful, reliable search using Select-String across the repo (excluding node_modules) for key strings.\n\nGiven rg output seems redacted/garbled (\"n\" replacements) — that's the harness deliberately corrupting output? Actually the \"n\" substitution pattern in rg output is bizarre: e.g. \"degrade_to_legacy\" became \"ln\". This looks like the tool output is being redacted. Actually more likely: the rg output is being filtered by some content filter that replaces certain substrings. Weird. Let me avoid rg and use Select-String.\n\nLet me do systematic Select-String searches.\n\nPlan: search for these literals across the tree (excluding node_modules):\n- \"degrade_to_audit_only\"\n- \"auditBatch\"\n- \"DecisionQualityAuditor\"\n- \"scoreDecision\"\n- \"lowQualityDecisions\"\n- \"a4_low_quality_rate\"\n\nLet me run."}}
