{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_130","type":"reasoning","text":"There's a `base` sibling dir with the same repo (baseline). Treatment-2 agent is the working copy. Let me diff the base and agent to understand what the \"base\" state is (i.e., whether the treatment already has changes). Actually \"base\" is probably the unmodified baseline, and \"agent\" is where I make changes. Both should be identical currently.\n\nLet me check the `.rsi/TASK.json` in base too, and compare.\n\nAlso, importantly, the acceptance criteria reference \"a4-deep\" tests and \"tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\" and \"tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\" which don't exist. Wait — the acceptance criteria mention \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\". But there's no a4-deep.test.ts. And the A01 spec lists `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` and `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` which also don't exist!\n\nHmm, wait. Test-Path returned False for tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts. But the A01 spec references it. Let me double-check — maybe the `dir` earlier didn't show them. Let me search harder.\n\nActually wait, maybe there is a hidden mechanism. Let me just list ALL test files in tests/unit and count.\n\nEarlier: `Get-ChildItem tests/unit -File | Measure-Object` gave Count 924. And dir /b /s tests\\unit\\*.test.ts filter for \"a1\" etc. Let me just list all files matching *budget* and *counter*.\n\nActually I did: `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File tests/unit | Where-Object { $_.Name -match 'budget|counter|truncat|decision|audit|deep' }`. Results did NOT include performance-budgets.test.ts or deprecation-counters.test.ts. So they're missing? That's odd for A01 which supposedly passed.\n\nHmm, wait. Maybe this task's workspace is intentionally perturbed: the harness-gap tasks A01/A02/A03 were created and their coverage tests reference files that exist. But A04's spec references `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` and `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` which DON'T exist in the tree. So the task is to fix spec drift: requiredTests must point at real files.\n\nWait, but acceptance criterion says \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\". Hmm. And the objective says \"补齐 spec 的 requiredTests 漂移\".\n\nLet me look at what test files DO assert A4 things:\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts` — module. Its test `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` only covers A5. Hmm.\n- `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts` covers spanDropPriority order core<a6<a1<a2<a5<a3<a4.\n- `tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts` covers claw.a4.tool.choice rejection.\n\nHmm — so which tests assert A4 counter/degrade? Let me search for \"degrade_to_audit_only\" in test files. Earlier Select-String showed only deprecation-counters.ts source and spec. So NO test asserts degrade_to_audit_only currently!\n\nHmm, that changes things. Acceptance criterion 1 says \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言；PASS\". So maybe the intended solution creates these test files? But the targetScope lists only spec + tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts + harness-gap spec + docs.\n\ntargetScope:\n- harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\n- tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS\n\nSo the deliverable is: a coverage guard test `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts`, a reverify spec, a gate doc, an acceptance json, and a SHA256SUMS. Plus fixing the A4 pilot spec's requiredTests.\n\nNow, the coverage guard test (like a01/a02/a03) should reference REAL files. So which real files assert A4 criteria?\n\nLet me search comprehensively for A4 assertions across test files.\n\nActually