04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` which the agent must CREATE.\n\nHold on. Let me reconsider. The `base` dir has those test files; the `agent` dir does not. So the harness removed from the agent workspace exactly the test files that are part of the hidden oracle. That means:\n- `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`\n- `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`\n- `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts`\n- `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`\n- `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`\n\nare the A04 hidden oracle tests. Wait, but those same files were also \"missing\" in tf-0293-a01 and tf-0294-a02 and tf-0295-a03 agent workspaces. So they're consistently held out across these gate tasks. Interesting: they are the shared \"A1-A4 gate evidence\" files.\n\nHmm, but wait — for tf-0293/tf-0294/tf-0295, base contains: counter, perf, trunc, auditor, a4deep = True. And agent contains only trunc, auditor, a4deep = True. So in A01/A02/A03 the held-out files were only counter+perf. For A04, additionally trunc, auditor, a4deep were held out too.\n\nHmm, this is confusing. Actually wait, tf-0295-a03 agent: trunc=True auditor=True a4deep=True? Let me recheck:\n```\ntf-0295-a03-treatment-1      agent  counter=False perf=False trunc=True auditor=True a4deep=True\n```\nYes. So for A01/A02/A03, only counter+perf were removed.\n\nAnd tf-0296-a04 agent: counter=False perf=False trunc=False auditor=False a4deep=False — five files removed.\n\nHmm OK so actually the file-set removal might be due to something else... maybe those files were created by *other* tasks in the dependency chain and just weren't present at this base commit? No — base HAS them.\n\nHold on, let me reconsider what \"base\" means. Maybe base is the *post-fix reference* (the \"gold\" repository after the correct solution), and agent is the pre-task state with certain files deleted to force the agent to recreate them?\n\nActually let me reconsider from the harness-design perspective. This is an RSI benchmark: for each tas