\n- tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts (existing)\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts (existing)\n- tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts (new)\n- tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts (new)\n- tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts (new, degradation order)\n\nAnd add a re-verification note section describing A04 outcome (residuals: production audit caller absent → NO-GO on production coverage; A4 not on production turn path → per-turn cumulative latency NOT-MEASURED).\n\nThe spec is `lifecycleStatus: archived`. Should I change lifecycleStatus? a01/a02/a03 specs remain `archived`. So keep archived, and add a \"Re-verification note (A04, 2026-10-13)\" section like a02 has.\n\n### 2. `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` (create)\nModel on a03's guard. Assertions:\n- requiredTests entries exist and include the auditor/a4-deep/deprecation-counters/trace-truncation tests.\n- deprecation-counters test asserts degrade_to_audit_only and lowQualityDecisions / 10%.\n- decision-quality-auditor test asserts auditBatch + lowQualityDecisions recording + flag-off parity (returns null when disabled) — but I can't read it. Hmm. I need to assert substrings that exist in that hidden test. Risky.\n\nHmm. This is the crux: my coverage guard must assert content of hidden tests. If I guess wrong, the guard fails.\n\nBut wait — maybe I don't need to assert hidden-test content. Let me design the guard to be robust:\n- Assert spec requiredTests include the expected paths (I control the spec).\n- Assert every requiredTests path exists (existsSync).\n- Assert A04 spec documents the residual (production audit caller absent, NO-GO) and the degradation order.\n- Assert the deprecation-counters source (not test) defines degrade_to_audit_only and the >10% threshold.\n- Assert the trace-truncation test file exists (degradation order evidence) — maybe just existence.\n- Assert the auditor source module implements auditBatch and flag-gating.\n\nThat way I assert on SOURCE files (which I c