wnership validation for the *reverify* spec (which owns the changed files). The reverify task spec's touchedAreas/ownedPaths must cover ALL changed files in my diff, or `validate` fails.\n\nChanged files in my diff:\n1. harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\n2. tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n3. harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md\n4. docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md\n5. docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json\n6. docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS\n7. Possibly docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS? (not required)\n\nI'll set ownedPaths to exactly those 6. Good.\n\nAlso harness validate runs with --since origin/main → no git repo here! `harness validate --spec X` without --no-diff uses git. But my workspace isn't a git repo (\"fatal: not a git repository\"). Let me check git.mjs handles absence gracefully.\n\nLet me check harness/src/git.mjs.\n\nAlso note: the AGENTS.md says validate real task specs without --no-diff. But no git → may fail. Let me check.\n\nLet me proceed to read git.mjs and cli.mjs validate path.\n\nAlso I should check the treatment `.rsi/AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` content: \"When a matching prior success/failure pair exists, compare both paths and preserve counterexamples before choosing the next action.\" This is the RSI treatment hint — suggesting I should compare a previous success and failure path. Interesting: maybe there are prior A04-ish trials. But that's a meta-instruction; I'll just do good work.\n\nLet me read git.mjs and cli validate."}}
