es to include the scenario's requiredRules? Let's check validateGatewayTaskSpec: requires scenario==gateway-backend-communication, taskType==runtime-bridge, requiredProfiles include ['fast','comms'], touchedAreas non-empty, expectedUserBehavior non-empty, acceptance non-empty, docs.required boolean, and requiredProfiles include scenario's requiredProfiles (fast, comms). Note: it does NOT require the scenario's requiredRules explicitly in validateTaskSpec... but cli.mjs for the *scenario* spec checks rules. For a task spec, no rule check. Hmm, but a01/a02/a03 reverify specs list requiredRules including backend-communication-boundary, comms-regression, docs-sync, task-forest-autoclose-and-roles, repository-artifact-retention. I'll mirror.\n\nAlso `validateChangedPathOwnership` with changedFiles=[] (since --no-diff) returns only residualPaths failures. So fine.\n\nNow, note: for the a4 pilot spec (`a4-decision-quality-pilot.md`), it already exists with `requiredTests` etc. I'll modify its requiredTests and add a re-verification note.\n\nLet me now check what the a3 spec looks like after drift fix (already in my workspace) — it has requiredTests including performance-budgets, anomaly-classifier, deprecation-counters, runtime deprecation-counters. And a03 reverify spec adds `tests/unit/a03-a3-gate-coverage.test.ts`. Note a03's *pilot* spec does NOT include the coverage guard in requiredTests; the *reverify* spec does. Good.\n\nSo mirroring:\n- a4 pilot spec requiredTests: tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts (original), + tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts, + tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts, + tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts, + tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts (degradation order). Keep the original entry first.\n- a04 reverify spec requiredTests: those + tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts.\n\nWait — a01's pilot spec requiredTests order: tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder, trace-namespace-enforcement, performance-budgets, deprecation-counters, runtime deprecation-counters (original entries first: tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter... hmm original a1 spec had those? Actually a01's drift was \"omitted the counter tests\". So original had tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder, trace-namespace-enforcement, performance-budgets; added deprecation-counters + runtime deprecation-counters.)\n\nFor a4, original requiredTests = performance-budgets.test.ts only (I saw that). Hmm wait, my workspace's a4 spec currently shows:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n```\nWait no! Let me re-read the very first cat of a4-decision-quality-pilot.md:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n```\nHmm, actually it said:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n```\nLet me scroll back... The output was:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n```\nHmm, I need to re-read. The first cat showed:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\nacceptance:\n  - A4 deprecation counter `lowQualityDecisions` rate ≤ 10% over audited decisions\n```\nHmm, wait, actually it showed `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` and `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`. Let me just re-read the file to be exact.\n\nLet me re-cat it.\n\nAlso I should double check the acceptance lines. Let me just re-read the file now.\n\nLet me also decide the retest of \"判据1 ... decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言；PASS（原门限未改）\". So criterion 1 maps to those three tests.\n\nLet me now write files. First re-read the a4 spec exactly.\n\nLet me proceed with commands.\n\nOne more: the SHA256SUMS format — `<hash>  <path>` two spaces. And it should include the 5-6 files: a4 pilot spec, a04 reverify spec, coverage test, gate doc, acceptance json. Looking at A03-SHA256SUMS: acceptance.json, gate.md, reverify spec, a3 pilot spec, coverage test. So 5 entries. I'll mirror: a04-acceptance.json, a04-decision-quality-gate.md, harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md, a4-decision-quality-pilot.md, tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts.\n\nNow, the ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS / e01 etc. — there's also a registry that may need updating? Let me check if there's a test that enumerates harness-gap-closure files (e.g., evidence-sha256sums.test.ts). Let me check that test to see if adding A04-SHA256SUMS requires registration.\n\nLet me look at tests/unit/evidence-sha256sums.test.ts.\n\nAlso check docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/baseline-acceptance.json for a registry of expected files. And there might be a test enumerating gate docs. Let me check.\n\nLet me run a few commands."}}
