{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_230","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"cd D:\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0296-a04-treatment-2\\\\agent; Get-Content harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\r\nlifecycleStatus: archived\r\nid: a4-decision-quality-pilot\r\ntitle: A4 Decision Quality — Active Pilot Gate\r\nscenario: gateway-backend-communication\r\ntaskType: runtime-bridge\r\nintent: Promote the A4 decision quality audit from shadow to active pilot, gated by audit coverage and budget compliance.\r\ntouchedAreas:\r\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts\r\nrequiredProfiles:\r\n  - fast\r\n  - comms\r\nrequiredRules:\r\n  - backend-communication-boundary\r\n  - comms-regression\r\nexpectedUserBehavior:\r\n  - With the A4 pilot gate enabled, decisions are audited and the low-quality counter stays at or under the 10% graduation budget.\r\n  - Every audited decision is covered in shadow mode (sampling rate 1.0) before the audit is treated as a gate.\r\n  - When the low-quality rate exceeds 10%, the pilot responds with `degrade_to_audit_only` instead of spending the rest of the turn budget.\r\n  - A4 degrades first in the documented order (A4→A3→A5→A1), so the per-turn cumulative latency budget is respected.\r\n  - With the pilot flag off, decision outcomes and the audit surface are unchanged.\r\nrequiredTests:\r\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\r\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\r\nacceptance:\r\n  - A4 deprecation counter `lowQualityDecisions` rate ≤ 10% over audited decisions\r\n  - A4 budget violation response `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when low-quality rate > 10%\r\n  - Per-turn cumulative latency budget respected (A4 is part of degradation order: A4→A3→A5→A1)\r\ndocs:\r\n  required: true\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Graduation gate\r\n\r\nA4 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:\r\n\r\n1. **Low-quality decision rate** ≤ 10%: `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`.\r\n2. **Audit coverage**: every decision is audited in shadow mode (sampling rate = 1.0).\r\n3. **Budget violation response**: `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when rate > 10% (criterion 4.14).\r\n4. **Per-turn cumulative budget**: A4 is the first to degrade (degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1).\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- Post-promotion sampling (OQ-004, Stage 5).\r\n- Decision quality scoring model (Stage 5 enhancement).\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_229","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"cd D:\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0296-a04-treatment-2\\\\agent; cat tests/unit/evidence-sha256sums.test.ts\"","aggregated_output":"// @vitest-environment node\r\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\r\nimport { mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\r\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\r\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\r\nimport { afterEach, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\r\nimport { verifyManifest } from '../../scripts/verify-evidence-sha256sums.mjs';\r\n\r\nconst roots: string[] = [];\r\nafterEach(() => {\r\n  for (const root of roots.splice(0)) rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\r\n});\r\n\r\nfunction setup() {\r\n  const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'evidence-sums-'));\r\n  roots.push(root);\r\n  const evidenceDir = join(root, 'artifacts', 'fixture');\r\n  mkdirSync(evidenceDir, { recursive: true });\r\n  writeFileSync(join(root, 'source.txt'), 'fixture', 'utf8');\r\n  const hash = createHash('sha256').update('fixture').digest('hex');\r\n  const manifest = join(evidenceDir, 'SHA256SUMS');\r\n  writeFileSync(manifest, `${hash}  source.txt\\n`, 'utf8');\r\n  return { root, evidenceDir, manifest };\r\n}\r\n\r\ndescribe('evidence SHA256SUMS verification (#70)', () => {\r\n  it('accepts a matching manifest', () => {\r\n    const { root, manifest } = setup();\r\n    const result = verifyManifest(root, manifest);\r\n    expect(result).toMatchObject({ checked: 1, matched: 1, missing: [], drifted: [] });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  it('accepts annotated historical drift and rejects unannotated drift', () => {\r\n    const { root, evidenceDir, manifest } = setup();\r\n    writeFileSync(join(root, 'source.txt'), 'changed', 'utf8');\r\n    expect(verifyManifest(root, manifest).drifted).toEqual(['source.txt']);\r\n    writeFileSync(join(evidenceDir, 'INTEGRITY.json'), JSON.stringify({\r\n      excludedEntries: [{ path: 'source.txt', reason: 'historical drift' }],\r\n    }), 'utf8');\r\n    expect(verifyManifest(root, manifest).annotatedDrift).toEqual(['source.txt']);\r\n    expect(verifyManifest(root, manifest).drifted).toEqual([]);\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_231","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I understand the task. Let me formulate the plan:\n\nDeliverables:\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md` — fix requiredTests drift (add auditor, a4-deep, degradation-order tests) + add A04 coverage guard note. Presumably add a re-verification note like a02/a03 and keep the thresholds unchanged.\n2. `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new coverage guard test\n3. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md` — the A04 spec (patterned on A03)\n4. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md` — the gate doc\n5. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json` — acceptance record\n6. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS` — sums\n\nThe withheld oracle test files: `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`, `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts`, `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`. The hidden oracle `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` is my deliverable.\n\nThe hidden oracle is likely `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — I write it, and they run all files including held-out ones.\n\nWait — the task says \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" So `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` is a deliverable I must write. The 5 withheld files are restored at eval time to check my coverage guard actually works. Note: `A03` tests `tests/unit/a03-a3-gate-coverage.test.ts` is in my workspace (I have it) since it's a previous lane's delivery.\n\nLet me check what the hidden A04 coverage test likely looks like based on A02/A03 patterns, and I must write a coverage guard that:\n- Asserts requiredTests entries exist\n- Pins the criterion-to-assertion mapping for A4 at original thresholds\n\nMy coverage guard must PASS with the held-out files present. But when I run now, they're absent — so my test will fail on `ex