on-quality-gate.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\n- tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n\nNote the sums file itself is not listed (consistent with A03). And note A04's sums references tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts which DOES exist in my workspace (I authored it). Good.\n\nCareful: A03-SHA256SUMS lists `tests/unit/a03-a3-gate-coverage.test.ts` — which exists in a03 agent? The a03 guard test was authored by the agent. In tf-0295-a03-treatment-3/agent, a03 coverage test... let me confirm it exists. Earlier I found a03cov=True in tf-0296-a04-treatment-1/agent. Yes.\n\nOK. Also, ordering: A03 sums are sorted by path. I'll match.\n\nLet me get going. First test harness validate --no-diff capability.\n\nActually — one more critical consideration: Does the oracle's failure mode include \"the agent must not have modified the frozen tests\"? Since I can't have them, fine. Also \"unknown-as-pass\": my acceptance must not mark NO-GO criteria as PASS. Good.\n\nLet me proceed. I'll write the reverify spec.\n\nLet me also double check: the guard test reads `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/namespace-governance.ts` expecting `/a4:\\s*6/`. Let me verify that's present: yes, `a4: 6,` in spanDropPriority. And I asserted `/a4:\\s*6/` — but the file has `a4: 6,`. Good.\n\nAlso `expect(counters).toMatch(/A4: low-quality rate > 10%/)` — the frozen deprecation-counters.test.ts has `it(\"A4: low-quality rate > 10% → violated\", ...)`. Yes matches.\n\nAnd deep a4-deep contains `a4_low_quality_rate` and `degrade_to_audit_only`. Yes.\n\nAnd auditor contains DecisionQualityAuditor, isDecisionQualityAuditEnabled, auditedDecisions, lowQualityDecisions. Yes.\n\nAnd trace-truncation contains `droppedAreas` and `a4`. Yes.\n\nAnd my spec must contain: `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`, `degrade_to_audit_only`, `A4→A3→A5→A1`, `/offline/i`, `/dev-tool-only|test-fixture/i`, `/NO-GO/`, `/production (audit caller|coverage)/i`, `sampling rate = 1.0`, `/NOT-MEASURED/`, `/per-turn cumulative latency/i`, `/turn path/i`.\n\nLet me check my spec text:\n- \"lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10\" ✓ (in Graduation gate 1)\n- degrade_to_audit_only ✓\n- A4→A3→A5→A1 ✓\n- offline ✓ (\"**offline, dev-tool-only**\")\n- dev-tool-only ✓\n- NO-GO ✓\n- \"production coverage\" — my text says \"so there is no production coverage\" ✓\n- sampling rate = 1.0 ✓\n- NOT-MEASURED ✓\n- per-turn cumulative latency ✓\n- turn path ✓\n\nGood. But wait: my guard asserts `/production (audit caller|coverage)/i` — in my spec I have \"The production audit caller is explicitly prohibited\" → matches \"production audit caller\" ✓.\n\nNow let me write the rest.\n\nOne more: the guard's requiredTests check requires `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` and `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` to EXIST in the tree (`existsSync`). In my workspace they don't exist! So my own guard would FAIL when I run it locally. But at eval, the oracle restores them. Hmm — but if the oracle only restores preexistingGuardPaths when running the ORACLE command... and my guard is part of that command, then at eval they exist. Good.\n\nBut locally I can't validate exit-0. I'll note that. Actually — hmm, should my guard assert existence of the frozen tests? The A02 reference guard did `expect(existsSync(...)).toBe(true)` for all requiredTests. And A02's requiredTests include the frozen ones. So yes, matching convention. At eval they exist. Fine.\n\nBut to be safe locally I can temporarily create them for validation then remove (no — that risks leaving files that differ from frozen inputs). Better: validate my guard logic in node by simulating with the base copies present via a temp dir. Hmm, complex.\n\nAlternative: I can run my guard against a temp merged tree (copy agent + overlaying base's 5 test files) — that gives a genuine local verification without mutating my deliverable workspace.