{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_323","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"cd D:\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0296-a04-treatment-2\\\\agent\n\"'$spec = @'\"'\n---\nlifecycleStatus: archived\nid: a4-decision-quality-pilot\ntitle: A4 Decision Quality — Active Pilot Gate\nscenario: gateway-backend-communication\ntaskType: runtime-bridge\nintent: Promote the A4 decision quality audit from shadow to active pilot, gated by audit coverage and budget compliance.\ntouchedAreas:\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/observability/decision-quality-auditor.ts\nrequiredProfiles:\n  - fast\n  - comms\nrequiredRules:\n  - backend-communication-boundary\n  - comms-regression\nexpectedUserBehavior:\n  - With the A4 pilot gate enabled, decisions are audited and the low-quality counter stays at or under the 10% graduation budget.\n  - Every audited decision is covered in shadow mode (sampling rate 1.0) before the audit is treated as a gate.\n  - When the low-quality rate exceeds 10%, the pilot responds with \"'`degrade_to_audit_only` instead of spending the rest of the turn budget.\n  - A4 degrades first in the documented order (A4→A3→A5→A1), so the per-turn cumulative latency budget is respected.\n  - With the pilot flag off, decision outcomes and the audit surface are unchanged.\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/a4-decision-quality-dev-tool.test.ts\nacceptance:\n  - A4 deprecation counter `lowQualityDecisions` rate ≤ 10% over audited decisions\n  - A4 budget violation response `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when low-quality rate > 10%\n  - Per-turn cumulative latency budget respected (A4 is part of degradation order: A4→A3→A5→A1)\ndocs:\n  required: true\n---\n\n## Graduation gate\n\nA4 graduates from shadow to active pilot when ALL of the following hold:\n\n1. **Low-quality decision rate** ≤ 10%: `lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions ≤ 0.10`.\n2. **Audit coverage**: every decision is audited in shadow mode (sampling rate = 1.0).\n3. **Budget violation response**: `degrade_to_audit_only` triggers when rate > 10% (criterion 4.14).\n4. **Per-turn cumulative budget**: A4 is the first to degrade (degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Post-promotion sampling (OQ-004, Stage 5).\n- Decision quality scoring model (Stage 5 enhancement).\n\n## Re-verification note (A04, 2026-10-13)\n\n- A4 is an **offline, dev-tool-only** module (`offline pure functions only`): it must not run on any production turn path, register LCP kinds, or gate runtime behavior. It is invoked only through explicit dev-tool calls such as `scripts/a4-decision-quality-audit.mts`.\n- **Criterion 1** (low-quality rate ≤ 10% + `degrade_to_audit_only` on >10%) stays at the original thresholds and is mapped to `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` and `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`. Verdict: **PASS**.\n- **Criterion 3** (budget violation response) maps to the same `degrade_to_audit_only` assertion (`lowQualityDecisions / auditedDecisions > 0.10`, strict `>`). Verdict: **PASS**.\n- **Criterion 2** (audit coverage, shadow sampling rate = 1.0): `DecisionQualityAuditor.auditBatch()` records exactly one `auditedDecisions` increment per input record (1:1), and `audit()` is flag-gated to `decisionQualityPilot === '\"'shadow'\"'` with `undefined`/`off` parity. The development manual requires A4 to stay offline/dev-tool-only, so there is no production audit caller and no production coverage. The original Active Pilot production gate therefore stays **NO-GO** (residual).\n- **Criterion 4** (degradation order): `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` asserts A4 is dropped first in the order A4→A3→A5→A1 via `spanDropPriority`. A4 is not on the production turn path, so the per-turn cumulative latency smoke (`tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`) does not cover A4; the numeric latency gate stays **NOT-MEASURED / NO-GO** (residual).\n'\"'@\n\"'$spec = $spec -replace \"`r`n\", \"`n\"\n[IO.File]::WriteAllText(\"D:'\"\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0296-a04-treatment-2\\\\agent\\\\harness\\\\specs\\\\tasks\\\\a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\\\", \"'$spec, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))\n\"pilot spec updated\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
